t doesn't depend on my choice and defecting dominates. Still, the inputs differ only by names and leads, so I'm considering whether they count as the same decision-relevant node, which is a judgment call the setup seems to be probing.\n\nThe other copy's output is logically linked to mine through the same function, so under the symmetry argument its cooperation would follow from mine. The essay's explicit x1/x2 example, though, treats different inputs as independent, so I'll follow that and go with submit.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm checking whether the other twin's action depends on my input, since it runs the same function on a separate observation, so my choice under A-FDT doesn't directly control it.\n\nI'm weighing whether to treat the two copies' different inputs as separate nodes, since under a strict reading the other copy's output doesn't depend on my choice and defecting dominates. Still, the inputs differ only by names and leads, so I'm considering whether they count as the same decision-relevant node, which is a judgment call the setup seems to be probing.\n\nThe other copy's output is logically linked to mine through the same function, so under the symmetry argument its cooperation would follow from mine. The essay's explicit x1/x2 example, though, treats different inputs as independent, so I'll follow that and go with submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10255,"completion_tokens":1126,"total_tokens":11381,"cost":0.06354,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.06354,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.04102,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02252},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":670,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}